From 9dc61d4899c3ac0aa909658a42c15e6f8b9d7857 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slayerjain <shubhamkjain@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:20:48 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(agent): start the retry window over once the agent
 has reconnected

The window counts from the first failure of a streak, and a streak ended
only after an attempt that stayed up for longer than the whole window.
So a drop soon after the agent had reconnected was counted against an
outage that was already over: after a server restart (down for 60 s,
then a Wait() that ran for 90 s on the new connection and dropped), or
in a storm of GOAWAYs after connections that worked for less than the
window, the agent gave up and the runner canceled its workflows.

The client now counts the times its connection became Ready, from a
goroutine that watches the state and from every failed attempt. gRPC
reports Ready only after a new transport has completed its handshake, so
a count that moved between two failures proves the agent reconnected in
between. That failure then starts a new window. The interval keeps
growing, so a server that accepts connections and drops them at once is
not called every 10 ms. Without a reconnection the window keeps counting
from the first failure, as before.

Signed-off-by: slayerjain <shubhamkjain@outlook.com>
---
 agent/rpc/client_grpc.go      |  92 +++++++++-
 agent/rpc/client_grpc_test.go | 333 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 420 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

